  ("Against the proposal", "loss of two-thirds of 40,000 books; value of browsing; elderly residents use it for company and newspapers; cost of 2.4 million and 18-month closure; equipment outdated in five years; the money could fund longer opening hours instead; fall in visitors caused by reduced hours; survey excluded older people."),
